{{ ansible_managed | comment }}
---
# Traefik dashboard on the platform Gateway's traefik listener. The listener
# terminates TLS at the edge with the pre-declared traefik-edge-tls secret
# (the cert-manager Gateway shim issues it from the listener, the same way
# as every other edge host); the cluster's CoreDNS answers
# traefik.k8s.dev.lo with the ingress address automatically.
#
# The backend is the rke2-traefik-dashboard Service, created by the
# rke2-traefik HelmChartConfig (service.additionalServices): it exposes the
# dashboard/API entrypoint of the rke2-traefik pods (container port 8080)
# as a ClusterIP, so the dashboard is reachable only through this route —
# never as a port on the LoadBalancer Service, which stays web/websecure.
# The dashboard UI (/) and its API (/api/...) both serve off that
# entrypoint, so this one route exposes both.
#
# The backend of the catch-all rule is the traefik-auth oauth2-proxy, not
# the dashboard Service: the dashboard has no authentication of its own, so
# SSO is enforced at the edge (sso.yaml), the estate's hubble-auth
# pattern. Unauthenticated requests are redirected to the Keycloak
# `traefik` client; a member of traefik-users or traefik-admins is
# admitted onto the rke2-traefik-dashboard Service behind the proxy.
# sso.yaml creates traefik-auth in kube-system, next to its backend.
#
# The exact-root rule below still lands on nothing: it is a pure
# redirect, so it does not bypass the proxy; /dashboard/ and everything
# else fall through to the catch-all and are session-checked there.
apiVersion: gateway.networking.k8s.io/v1
kind: HTTPRoute
metadata:
  name: traefik-dashboard
  namespace: kube-system
spec:
  parentRefs:
    - name: platform
      namespace: kube-system
      sectionName: traefik
  hostnames:
    - traefik.{{ inventory_gitops_source_cluster_domain }}
  rules:
    # The dashboard UI serves at /dashboard/ (its assets and /api are
    # path-relative to that prefix), so the bare host root is a permanent
    # redirect to /dashboard/. It is done here, at the TLS-terminating
    # listener, so the redirect stays https: the plain-HTTP dashboard
    # entrypoint behind the backend hop would otherwise emit an http://
    # Location (its internal dashboard_redirect middleware is bound to the
    # scheme the entrypoint sees, which is plain HTTP behind the edge), and
    # the browser would follow it to port 80 and 404.
    - matches:
        - path:
            type: Exact
            value: /
      filters:
        - type: RequestRedirect
          requestRedirect:
            path:
              type: ReplaceFullPath
              replaceFullPath: /dashboard/
    - backendRefs:
        - name: traefik-auth
          port: 80
